# Per run of each corpus program (scripts/compile-corpus.sh, `bcc-counts`): allocations, indirect (dispatched) calls and copies at a non-trivial type,
# at the flat IR and Wasm; and, at the flat IR, loads (each `load`/`load8` evaluated), stores (each `store`/`store8` run; heap and frame slots, never
# locals) and bounds checks (each test of an index against an array's length an access makes: `idx`, `split`, a literal's byte; not a loop's end test).
